  "observation": "The historical tree-hash benchmark uses Keccak-f[800]: 25 lanes of 32 bits and 22 rounds. It is not the 1600-bit SHA-3 sponge. Its source layout is part of the contract: the CPU root absorbs contiguous eight-word chunks from the actual structure-of-arrays leaf buffer. Each measured pipeline includes H2D transfer, leaf hashing, D2H transfer, and CPU root work across eight passes whose root state carries forward. Consequently these are pipeline timings, not device-only hash throughput. Full leaf chaining words and every 25-lane root state are compared. An independent coordinate-form permutation with LFSR-generated constants is first checked against two published XKCP known answers, then used for complete measured-output verification. No assertion about standardized tree hashing, padding, domain separation, or cryptographic security follows from this numerical agreement.",
